-- title:
--   Base change of the j-finite chart ring to a ramified DVR
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero natural number $N$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N$, and let $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ denote [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8), the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $K'$ be an intermediate field of $L((q))/L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma0 (N * p)))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the subfield of $L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images under `coeffEmb L` of the elements of the $q$-expansion field $\mathbb{Q}$-generated by `intFormRatiosC ℚ (Gamma0 (N*p))`. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an algebra structure over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ and over which $L$ is the fraction field, compatibly, with $p$ lying in the maximal ideal of $A$; let $K'$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K'$. Let $j' \in K'$ be nonzero with underlying Laurent series `coeffEmb L jq`. Then there is an $A$-algebra isomorphism $$A \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}} \mathrm{chartAlgFin}(Np,p) \;\xrightarrow{\sim}\; \mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin}\,A\,K'\,j',$$ from the base change of the $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-subalgebra of elements of `modularFunctionFieldFull (N*p)` integral over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[j]$ to the $A$-subalgebra of $K'$ of elements integral over $A[j']$, such that for every $b$ in the source chart ring, the image of $1 \otimes b$ in $L((q))$ is the coefficientwise image `coeffEmb L` of the $q$-expansion of $b$.
--
--   This identifies the $j$-finite chart ring of the two-chart integral model of the base-changed modular function field of $\Gamma_0(Np)$ over a possibly ramified discrete valuation ring $A$ with the base change of the corresponding chart ring of the Igusa scheme over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$, compatibly with $q$-expansions. It is used in the analysis of the minimal primes above $p$ in the chart ring of $X_0(Np)$, in the lemmas [`ModularCurve.XZeroP.le_of_mem_minimalPrimes_span_of_mem_ssJSet_chartAlgFin_gamma0_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XZeroP.le_of_mem_minimalPrimes_span_of_mem_ssJSet_chartAlgFin_gamma0_mul) and [`ModularCurve.XZeroP.map_jChartFin_mem_ssJSet_of_exists_two_minimalPrimes_span_le_chartAlgFin_gamma0_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XZeroP.map_jChartFin_mem_ssJSet_of_exists_two_minimalPrimes_span_le_chartAlgFin_gamma0_mul).
